.TH BF 1
.SH NAME
bf \- run a Brainfuck program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bf
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute the Brainfuck source in FILE. With no argument, print a short usage
message. Non-command characters are ignored, and brackets are checked before
execution. Programs may contain up to 30000 instructions.
.PP
The tape has 30000 initially zero cells. Cell values wrap from 255 to 0 and
back; the tape pointer wraps at either end. The comma command reads standard
input, storing zero at EOF. The dot command writes standard output.
.SH EXAMPLE
bf /hello.bf
